  "summary": "Recent preprints report modulated optical drives reaching cavity-bandwidth amplitude limits and sub-quantum-backaction cooling.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is time-dependent optical driving used to shape optomechanical backaction. One preprint shows that intensity-modulated driving near the mechanical resonance raises oscillation amplitude toward the cavity-bandwidth limit and widens the frequency comb bandwidth. Another reports that Floquet driving in multimode optomechanical resonators reverses dynamical backaction and cools an MHz mode to 47 phonons below the quantum backaction limit. Both works therefore treat modulation of the optical drive as the control parameter for mechanical dynamics. A third preprint, on mode-locking in liquid light, applies a hydrodynamic framework to phase dynamics of fast-gain lasers and shares only the general theme of driven optical phase dynamics, not the optomechanical mechanism.",
